<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Low rainfall and hot weather had accelerated the development of Argentina's 1996/97 soybean crop, especially double crop beans, by April 4, the Agriculture Secretariat said in weekly crop report Thursday.</p>
<p>Stress from lack of moisture during a long stretch of the crop cycle also affected pod-filling. There are relatively few, and smallish, beans in each pod. Large parts of the soybean area needed rain soon to partially revive the crop. With 7.5 percent of the soybeans harvested, early yields have been patchy and lower than expected. Beans have ranged in size from medium to small, the Secretariat said.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..................Yield</p>
<p> Wheat     6,983  100.0(100.0) 6,694.4  100.0   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Maize     3,890  100.0(100.0) 1,423.8   40.6  (31.3)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Soybeans  6,583  100.0(100.0)   491.4    7.5   (2.5)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sunflower 3,075  100.0(100.0) 2,514.1   84.4  (85.1)    (n/a)</p>
